        "title": "Add welcome invite via parameter constants to product funnel schema",
        "summary": "Two new exported constants, `WELCOME_INVITE_VIA_PARAM` and `WELCOME_INVITE_VIA`, were added to the product funnel schema in the `common` package. The via query parameter identifies the specific share method that generated a Desktop welcome invite link, allowing analytics to tie the invitee's signup back to the inviter's action. The constants define the query string key and the enumerated values for email and link shares, while the accompanying comment notes this mechanism deliberately avoids using standard UTM parameters to preserve the account's first-touch channel classification as a referral.",
